📄 10_error_propagation_flow.puml
How errors move through UI → ViewModel → Logic → Platform → back to UI
plantuml
@startuml
title Error Propagation Across Layers (UI → VM → Logic → Platform →
VM → UI)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
actor User
participant "UI Layer\n(Compose)" as UI
participant "ViewModel\n(ui-shared)" as VM
participant "Shared Logic\n(core)" as Logic
participant "Platform Services\n(Android/Desktop)" as Platform
== User Action ==
User -> UI: Trigger action
UI -> VM: onEvent(Event)
== ViewModel Delegates Work ==
VM -> Logic: performOperation()
== Shared Logic Calls Platform ==
Logic -> Platform: platformCall()
Platform --> Logic: error/exception
== Logic Handles Error ==
Logic -> Logic: wrap error\n(domain-specific error)
Logic --> VM: return Failure(error)
== ViewModel Reduces Error ==
VM -> VM: update state to ErrorState
VM --> UI: emit Effect(ShowError)
== UI Displays Error ==
UI -> User: show error message
@enduml
This diagram helps you reason about:
• Where errors originate
• How they propagate
• Where they’re transformed
• How they surface in UI
It’s invaluable when debugging.
📄 11_glossary_of_architecture_terms.puml
A visual glossary of the architectural vocabulary your project uses
plantuml
@startuml
title Glossary of Architectural Terms (Visual Map)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
package "Glossary" {
 class UI {
 note right
 The Compose UI layer.
 Renders state and sends events.
 end note
 }
 class ViewModel {
 note right
 Holds state.
 Processes events.
 Calls shared logic.
 Emits effects.
 end note
 }
 class State {
 note right
 Immutable UI state.
 Produced by the ViewModel.
 end note
 }
 class Event {
 note right
 User or system actions.
 Sent from UI to ViewModel.
 end note
 }
 class Effect {
 note right
 One-time actions:
 navigation, toasts, dialogs.
 end note
 }
 class SharedLogic {
 note right
 Platform-agnostic logic.
 Audio pipeline, storage abstraction,
 transcription controller.
 end note
 }
 class PlatformService {
 note right
 Android/Desktop implementations
 of shared interfaces.
 end note
 }
 class DI {
 note right
 Koin modules that wire
 shared and platform layers.
 end note
 }
}
UI --> ViewModel
ViewModel --> State
UI --> Event
ViewModel --> Effect
ViewModel --> SharedLogic
SharedLogic --> PlatformService
DI --> ViewModel
DI --> PlatformService
@enduml